# UX contract (onsocial-app)

Goal: every screen feels instant and stable. Zero layout shift, bounded memory, one motion style. Match or beat best-in-class apps on feel; get there through the primitives below, not by replacing them.

## Before you implement

- Read the code you'll touch and its callers first; note existing bugs, races, stale-request commits, or layout shift in that area. Fix those in scope as part of the change; list out-of-scope findings in the PR description rather than fixing them silently.
- For any non-trivial UI/UX or data-flow change, briefly identify the industry best-in-class approach to the same problem and pick the one that feels most premium: instant, stable, smooth, minimal.
- Then implement that approach through the existing primitives below. If they can't reach it, stop before building and say why (what falls short, with evidence, and the proposed extension or replacement); don't build a parallel system or replace a primitive without approval.
- State the chosen approach and why in the PR description.

## Use what exists; never add a parallel system

- Before using Next.js APIs, read the matching guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (this Next version differs from training data).
- No `framer-motion` (portal-only), `react-query`, `SWR`, `react-window`, or parallel UI systems.
- Navigation, lists, and prefetch: `OsRouteSettle`, `useFeedWindow`, `useListScrollRestore`, `IntentPrefetchHost`.
- Seeds: `home-feed-session`, `PortfolioProfileSeed`, `standing-list-cache`, `writing-shelf-warm`, `launcher-mine-session`, `launcher-latest-session`.
- Sheets: `OsHugSheet`, `OsGestureSheet`, or `GlassSheet`.
- Follow sibling rules by concern (do not duplicate or invent alternatives): `app-loading-contract.mdc` (with `app-loading-contract.ts` + `app-loading-matrix.ts`), `app-button-toast-contract.mdc`, `app-chrome-spacing.mdc`, `app-dao-face.mdc`, `app-empty-copy.mdc`, `app-mage-icons.mdc`, `hug-drawer-actions.mdc`, `app-gesture-opens-surface.mdc`, `app-indexer-first-paint.mdc`, `app-portfolio-face.mdc`, and `implement-clean.mdc`.

## Viewer mood on OS shells

Portfolio and wallet mood live in `app-portfolio-face.mdc`. These shells only:

- `OsAppScreen` and `OsSlideOverScreen` apply the connected **viewer** mood by default (`useViewerDockMood`). Do not re-thread `moodId` / `moodStyle` on every panel. `moodId={null}` keeps the blue-corner trial. Pass an explicit mood only as a rare override.
- Outside those shells (compose post, manage flows, account sheets): resolve CSS vars (`portfolioMoodShellStyle` or the viewer hook `style`) and pass `moodId` + `moodStyle`, or omit them and let the shells default. Prefer a subtle `--mood-bg` under translucent glass — opaque glass that hides the wash does not count.
- Compose and slide-over wash stays inside the app column on phone. Desktop gutters stay OS `--bg` (no outside mood glow). A slide-over clears card radius so host glow cannot bleed. The portfolio hairline ban is in `app-portfolio-face.mdc`.
- `guild-composer-sheet` may still pass viewer mood explicitly. Most routes inherit `OsAppScreen`.

## Stacked overlays and Back

When a drawer (or any nested overlay) sits on top of a sheet or another overlay, Back closes the **topmost** surface first. The sheet or page underneath stays until that top surface is gone. Drawers take navigation priority over the sheet they cover; the same rule applies to any future stacked overlay (drawer over sheet, sheet over sheet, modal over drawer). Do not wire dock Back, header Back, or browser Back so the underlay dismisses while a drawer above it is still open.

Place stack history: each opened post, quotes, or drop screen **pushes** one native history entry, including the first open from home. Browser Back, dock Back, and header Back each close only the top screen. Native history only — App Router push would remount and kill the feed underlay.

Summon dock auto-hide follows the top screen's scroller. A covered screen's scroll does not tuck it. Opening or closing the top screen shows the dock again.

## Motion

- Content appear / route settle: `var(--os-motion-appear)` (280ms) + `var(--os-motion-ease-standard)`.
- **Warm drop open is opaque, one mount.** Soft tap opens `DropLayerSheet` (`presentation="appear"`, dock Back + Mint) over the underlay — native history only, same stack as posts. Seed / view cache / now-playing paint solid with no skeleton and no surface fade — Collectibles / Show pass must not remount. Soft-fill updates that same embedded panel after first paint. Cold miss: panel `OsRouteSettle` + four-block rise once under the cover, then drop the rise class when the animation ends (timer fallback). Under cold settle, suppress a second page-wide body fade (rise owns entrance). Hard refresh / share keep the real `/collection/[id]` route (SSR). No InstantHost dual paint. Other pages do not add a per-block rise.
- Late seats: prefer reserved geometry + instant swap; never fade soft-fill into a reserved seat. `OsPageBodyAppear` for a true late seat only when there was no prior skeleton. A wallet line that can wrap reserves its final in-flow box up front.
- Scale: micro 120, chip 160, chrome 220, dock 260, overlay 320, `ease-out` (glass-sheet), `ease-soft` (expand / collapse), `ease-slide`.
- No raw durations or cubic-beziers. Opacity only on nodes containing the fixed dock.
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: no appear animation (`OsRouteSettle` drops the cover immediately; the drop rise does not run; appear keyframes live under `no-preference`).

## Loading

Owned by `app-loading-contract.mdc` (+ `app-loading-contract.ts`, `app-loading-matrix.ts`). Do not restate it here.

## Layout stability

- Every image/video has a reserved height or `aspect-ratio` before decode.
- Async UI (wallet state, counts, chips, banners) reserves its final size up front; swaps never change height.
- Fonts via `next/font/local` only (`src/fonts/index.ts`; `next/font/google` is ESLint-banned).

## Lists and data

- Lists that can exceed 12 rows use `useFeedWindow` (`FEED_WINDOW_MIN_COUNT = 12`). Stable id keys (`[data-feed-key]`); index keys only for static placeholders.
- Pagination: keyset only for feed lists (`HomeFeedPageCursor.beforeBlockHeight` / `beforeEventHeat` / `beforeEventKey` — Recent, Pulse, and Hot Global/Circle heat). Incomplete edges end the walk — never page a keyset feed by `nextOffset` / list length.
- Async load, refresh, and append results commit only if `isCurrentLoadingRequest(loadId)`. Realtime subscribe handlers patch or reload directly without that gate.
- Lists a user can leave and return to use `useListScrollRestore`. Don't set `history.scrollRestoration`.

## Code and done means

- Minimal diffs, no dead code, concise why-only inline docs.
- CLS 0 on the portfolio face (`PerformanceObserver` probe in `e2e/portfolio-pill.spec.ts`); aim under 0.1 elsewhere.
- Long scroll keeps `[data-feed-key]` count bounded (`e2e/feed-windowing.spec.ts`).
- Typecheck (`pnpm --filter @onsocial/app run type-check`) and touched tests pass; push with `PRE_PUSH_E2E=0` — CI is the gate.
